MID_EV30_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_015_m01_001: Ill news. The remaining gates of the underworld\nare all showing signs of activity at once.
MID_EV30_015_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_002: Everything hinges on what we do next. We mustn't\nlose sight of the goal.
MID_EV30_015_m01_003: Feels like our enemies have gotten more and more\nactive lately, doesn't it?
MID_EV30_015_m01_004: This is gonna be tough. I hope we can destroy\nthem all.
MID_EV30_015_m01_005: <NCA>"Are you worried?"
MID_EV30_015_m01_006: <NCB>"I have faith in us."
MID_EV30_015_m01_007: <ACA>Yeah... But we don't have a choice. The fate of the\nwhole world is at stake.
MID_EV30_015_m01_008: <ACB>Knowing you feel that way makes me think we'll get\nthrough this.
MID_EV30_015_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_014: Balor will want as many souls as he can feast on\nbefore the eclipse.
MID_EV30_015_m01_015: And for him to claim those souls, the gates must\nmanifest to send his forces out into our world.
MID_EV30_015_m01_016: There is risk in it for him, yes, but he is willing to\nchance it to gain greater power.
MID_EV30_015_m01_017: That said, he will do whatever he can to minimize\nthat risk.
MID_EV30_015_m01_018: We will face his most powerful gatekeepers who\nprotect the few gates that remain.
MID_EV30_015_m01_019: What say you to that? Can we still prevail?
MID_EV30_015_m01_020: <NCA>"With ease."
MID_EV30_015_m01_021: <NCB>"We'll do what we must."
MID_EV30_015_m01_065: <ACA>
MID_EV30_015_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_066: <ACB>
MID_EV30_015_m01_023: <ACB>It is as you say, Promised One. No matter the\nopponent, they will be cut down.
MID_EV30_015_m01_024: That's the spirit. Lead us all to victory,\nPromised One.
MID_EV30_015_m01_025: I don't think there's anything more dispiriting than\nspeaking with the risen dead.
MID_EV30_015_m01_026: Especially when they're people you knew when\nthey were alive...
MID_EV30_015_m01_027: Once we destroy these gates, our preparations will\nbe complete.
MID_EV30_015_m01_028: After that, all that will be left is the final reckoning\nwith Balor. Although...
MID_EV30_015_m01_031: <NCA>"Is there a problem?"
MID_EV30_015_m01_032: <NCB>"Is something bothering you?"
MID_EV30_015_m01_033: Mmm. 'Tis not worth mentioning.
MID_EV30_015_m01_034: Even consumed by madness as he is, Balor will be\na deadly opponent.
MID_EV30_015_m01_035: We have robbed some of his strength by destroying\nthe gates, but he has power still to spare.
MID_EV30_015_m01_036: You once referred to Balor and Dagda as special\nbeings known as Founders.
MID_EV30_015_m01_037: And yet we have already bested Dagda. If Balor is of\nsimilar prowess, he will fall as well.
MID_EV30_015_m01_038: Indeed you did vanquish Dagda, but I caution you\nthat Balor is another story.
MID_EV30_015_m01_039: Though Dagda enjoyed the benefits of flamma,\nits use dulled his mind. And that's not all.
MID_EV30_015_m01_040: The power that Dagda wielded has been subsumed\ninto Balor and added to his own.
MID_EV30_015_m01_041: His strength grows even as we speak. I must warn\nyou not to take him lightly.
MID_EV30_015_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_044: You should know that originally, the progenitor god\ncouldn't have children by mating with others.
MID_EV30_015_m01_045: She suspected the information contained in her body\nwas too complex for that.
MID_EV30_015_m01_046: So she split that information into seven parts and\ncombined them with human tissue.
MID_EV30_015_m01_047: This resulted in seven children—the Founders, also\nknown as the first seven.
MID_EV30_015_m01_048: I see. These Founders are the beings closest in \nnature to the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_015_m01_049: This makes me want to fight Balor, and quickly.\nOh, yes.
MID_EV30_015_m01_050: Her current children—the Nabateans—came from\nthese first seven multiplying with others.
MID_EV30_015_m01_051: Most Nabateans possess a single Diadem. But the\nFounders lay claim to more.
MID_EV30_015_m01_052: The Diadems are the power of the progenitor god,\nsplit into 21 parts. Each of the seven has three.
MID_EV30_015_m01_053: A Diadem's power is handed down through\nbloodlines, but it gradually weakens.
MID_EV30_015_m01_054: And 'tis not only the Diadems that ebb.
MID_EV30_015_m01_055: We, her children, grow weaker with each generation,\nand our lifespans gradually shorten as well.
MID_EV30_015_m01_056: Seen in that light, we Nabateans are merely another\nspecies destined for extinction.
MID_EV30_015_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_015_m01_060: Only the progenitor god knows why we children\nwere given life.
MID_EV30_015_m01_061: But 'tis not such a great problem. Nothing is\neternal, after all.
MID_EV30_015_m01_062: Our eventual extinction is not a directive to die.
MID_EV30_015_m01_063: 'Tis the opposite, in fact. She is spurring us to live\nwithin the time we have.
MID_EV30_015_m01_064: Only recently have I come to see it in this way.
MID_EV30_116_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_116_m01_001: Hrm...
MID_EV30_116_m01_002: Oh, 'tis you again. I was pondering certain matters.
MID_EV30_116_m01_003: <NCA>"I could tell something is bothering you."
MID_EV30_116_m01_004: <NCB>"You seemed distracted at the war council."
MID_EV30_116_m01_005: <ACA>I suppose so. There is a fear I've not been able to\nquiet for some time now.
MID_EV30_116_m01_006: <ACB>Noticed that, did you? You are a perceptive one.
MID_EV30_116_m01_007: <ACB>Yes... There is something that's been troubling me\nfor a while.
MID_EV30_116_m01_008: And I'm no closer than I was to a solution.
MID_EV30_116_m01_009: <NCA>"I'm here if you want to talk."
MID_EV30_116_m01_010: 'Tis all of you that I fear for.
MID_EV30_116_m01_011: As I said, there is only one way to destroy Balor.
MID_EV30_116_m01_013: We must enter the underworld from his temple and\nattack him directly.
MID_EV30_116_m01_014: And there's the rub. The underworld is by nature\ncontained within Balor himself.
MID_EV30_116_m01_015: What, then, when Balor is destroyed? 'Tis safe to\nassume his underworld will collapse with him.
MID_EV30_116_m01_016: Do you see the problem? If we are in the underworld\nwhen it ceases to exist...
MID_EV30_116_m01_017: Even I cannot fathom what might become of those\nwho dared set foot inside.
MID_EV30_116_m01_018: <NCA>"Hmm."
MID_EV30_116_m01_019: At best, we may find ourselves...nowhere. At worst,\nwe could be snuffed out completely.
MID_EV30_116_m01_020: These people have risked their lives to fight an\nimpossible struggle.
MID_EV30_116_m01_021: When the time comes...can I give the order, knowing\nwhat I know?
MID_EV30_116_m01_022: I find that I've grown more fond of all of you than\nI thought.
MID_EV30_116_m01_023: All I want is for you to live full lives—even you,\nwho already died once.
MID_EV30_116_m01_024: If only I could think of something to do about it.\nThere must be a way!
MID_EV30_116_m01_025: <NCA>"I'm sure we'll be alright."
MID_EV30_116_m01_026: <NCB>"If there isn't, then maybe..."
MID_EV30_116_m01_027: <ACA>Death seems to have left you with an oddly sunny\ndisposition.
MID_EV30_116_m01_028: <ACA>I find it...cheering, of late.
MID_EV30_116_m01_029: <ACB>Don't tell me you intend to go in on your own.
MID_EV30_116_m01_030: <ACB>For one thing, it wouldn't work. The two of us alone\nwouldn't be enough to face him.
MID_EV30_116_m01_031: <ACB>We'll need everyone to contribute if we hope to\nsave this world.
MID_EV30_116_m01_032: Yet something must be done, I admit.
MID_EV30_116_m01_033: Unless we destroy Balor, this world is doomed.\nOur options are therefore limited.
MID_EV30_116_m01_034: For now, we must turn our attention to the gates.\nAnd in the meantime, I'll continue my pondering.
MID_EV30_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_022_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_082: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_083: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_084: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_085: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_086: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_087: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_088: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_001: 'Tis absurdly hot here. What an annoying place\nto put a gate.
MID_EV30_022_m01_002: I'll persevere, but my head is starting to swim.
MID_EV30_022_m01_003: <NCA>"Are you sure you're OK?"
MID_EV30_022_m01_004: Perhaps it's the rancid air from these geysers.
MID_EV30_022_m01_005: Fortuna, Promised One, I'd ask that you be cautious.
MID_EV30_022_m01_006: There's a reason locals call this place the Valley\nof Death.
MID_EV30_022_m01_007: Even beasts don't call it home.
MID_EV30_022_m01_008: <NCA>"You know a lot about this place."
MID_EV30_022_m01_009: Yes. Father Mahdel's shrine, where I lived in hiding\nwhen I was a child—it's nearby.
MID_EV30_022_m01_010: I've found it hard to breathe for a while now.\nI guess those geysers are why.
MID_EV30_022_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_013: Hmph. We ought not to linger here. Let's destroy the\ngate quickly so we can leave.
MID_EV30_022_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_017: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_025: C'mon, we learned our lesson! We'll never touch\nyour treasure again!
MID_EV30_022_m01_026: Yep—in fact we'll never even come anywhere near it.\nPlease! You gotta let us go!
MID_EV30_022_m01_027: End them.
MID_EV30_022_m01_028: Gyaaaah!
MID_EV30_022_m01_029: Hehehehe... HAHAHAHA!
MID_EV30_022_m01_030: There'll be no mercy for anyone who lays a finger on\nmy treasures.
MID_EV30_022_m01_031: Every mangy dog who tries it will be hurled straight\nto the bottom of the valley.
MID_EV30_022_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_032: We're too late. They may have been thieves...but it's\nunfortunate we could not save them.
MID_EV30_022_m01_033: You there! More bandits out to steal what's mine, eh?
MID_EV30_022_m01_089: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_034: Whoa! We've been spotted!
MID_EV30_022_m01_035: Big voice, big man. Wow.
MID_EV30_022_m01_036: A massive opponent who carries the scent of\nthe strong.
MID_EV30_022_m01_037: He is worthy to face my blade. Do your best, and I\nmay enjoy this.
MID_EV30_022_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_041: Listen well and remember... I alone am the richest\nman in all of Dagda!
MID_EV30_022_m01_042: Thieves upon thieves. I won't let any of you steal\na single gold piece from my treasury!
MID_EV30_022_m01_043: This is unlike the Brimstone Lords we have faced.\nI do not understand his strong fixation with gold.
MID_EV30_022_m01_044: Nevertheless, our goal has not changed. Whoever this\nman was, we must defeat him.
MID_EV30_022_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_062: <NCA>"Prepare for battle."
MID_EV30_022_m01_063: That's right. We've come to destroy the underworld\ngate—just as soon as we dispatch you.
MID_EV30_022_m01_064: What?! I'll make you eat those words. Nobody talks\nthat way to the mighty Drake!
MID_EV30_022_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_065: So you are the pirate Drake, are you?
MID_EV30_022_m01_066: Many Saraminians saw you as a hero—the rare noble\nthief of legend.
MID_EV30_022_m01_067: But perhaps we deluded ourselves out of bitterness\ntoward the temples.
MID_EV30_022_m01_068: We so wanted the enemy of our enemy to be our\nfriend that we overlooked your true character.
MID_EV30_022_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_022_m01_074: I do detest this man. So loud...so overbearing.
MID_EV30_022_m01_075: Let's show this Brimstone Lord that we don't make\nempty threats!
MID_EV30_023_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_023_m01_001: Noooooo! My treasuuure!
MID_EV30_023_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_002: Get your filthy hands off it! I won't give it up...\nnot to anyone... IT'S MIIIIIINE!
MID_EV30_023_m01_003: My goodness, but he was a greedy one to the end.
MID_EV30_023_m01_004: He was twisted, but remained true to himself to\nthe last.
MID_EV30_023_m01_005: Such was the foe I faced today. I have no cause\nfor complaint.
MID_EV30_023_m01_006: Nothing shakes you, does it? The most terrifying\nthings happen and you stay firm.
MID_EV30_023_m01_007: I'm surprised to realize that I'm a little envious.
MID_EV30_023_m01_008: Hm.
MID_EV30_023_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_009: This is a lot of treasure. What do we do with it?
MID_EV30_023_m01_010: Seems like we could find a good use for it.
MID_EV30_023_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_014: This hoard would be best put to use purchasing\nfood and equipment for any surviving settlements.
MID_EV30_023_m01_015: <NCA>"I agree."
MID_EV30_023_m01_016: We can enlist the priests to start making the\nnecessary arrangements.
MID_EV30_023_m01_017: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_033: I suppose we all have to come to terms with it—that\nwe can't stay children forever.
MID_EV30_023_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_023_m01_046: All people covet what others have.
MID_EV30_023_m01_047: 'Tis greed to see everyone's grass as greener.\nBut 'tis also greed to fence in one's own field.
MID_EV30_023_m01_048: Yet that vice is a strong driver of human progress.
MID_EV30_023_m01_049: Our Brimstone Lord friend seemed to have an\noverdeveloped sense of it.
MID_EV30_023_m01_050: If people would cease comparing their wealth to one\nanother, they'd not be so fixated on such things.
MID_EV30_023_m01_051: I suspect there is a reason people obsess over what\nthey see and cannot have.
MID_EV30_023_m01_052: 'Tis a lack of love for themselves.
MID_EV30_023_m01_053: Cause and effect... We are all of us ill-starred\ncreatures indeed.
MID_EV30_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_024_m01_001: Dear me! What is this place?
MID_EV30_024_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_002: Everywhere I step, there's a crumbled stone in\nmy path.
MID_EV30_024_m01_003: That's when the grass and vines aren't tripping\nme up.
MID_EV30_024_m01_004: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_005: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_006: This region was host to ancient ruins by the name\nof Kurdelind.
MID_EV30_024_m01_007: Supposedly they belonged to a civilization that\nflourished here before the Mosa first appeared.
MID_EV30_024_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_013: When chased, people flee, fight, and fall...leaving\nonly traces behind.
MID_EV30_024_m01_014: This is the way of things—anywhere, anywhen.
MID_EV30_024_m01_015: Damn Balor for summoning an underworld gate all\nthe way out here.
MID_EV30_024_m01_016: 'Tis a long march on our way to destroy each one.\nI've a mind to tell him to try the trek himself.
MID_EV30_024_m01_017: Uh... I doubt he responds to being chastised.
MID_EV30_024_m01_018: It would be strange if Balor made it easy for us.
MID_EV30_024_m01_019: Quiet... I think I hear something.
MID_EV30_024_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_022: Those are sounds of a struggle. Let us move quickly\nto their aid.
MID_EV30_024_m01_023: My own warriors were not deployed here. Could this\nbe the Mosa under siege?
MID_EV30_024_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_024: General Klapka, it's no use. We're vastly\noutnumbered!
MID_EV30_024_m01_025: If we can't turn the tide, it won't be long before they\nbreak through here.
MID_EV30_024_m01_026: Tell the men to fight harder. Hold nothing back!\nIf we fall here, our doom is sealed.
MID_EV30_024_m01_027: Y-yes, sir!
MID_EV30_024_m01_028: This underworld gate...what have those northerners\ngone and done now?
MID_EV30_024_m01_029: The armies of the dead have spilled over into our\ncountry, causing no end of chaos.
MID_EV30_024_m01_030: The king sent us out here to stop them before they\ncould overrun the holy city of Halkaparikke.
MID_EV30_024_m01_031: But I don't see how we have a hope of that. It's only\na matter of time before they wipe us out.
MID_EV30_024_m01_032: I've never seen a more fearsome opponent. That\nBrimstone Lord is a living embodiment of wrath.
MID_EV30_024_m01_033: Typical of those Saraminians to vanish after bringing\nthis calamity down on our heads!
MID_EV30_024_m01_034: Though if they showed up now to help turn the tide,\nI wouldn't say no.
MID_EV30_024_m01_035: Oh? I recognize that general.
MID_EV30_024_m01_036: Even the elites among the Mosa warriors seem to be\nstruggling against the risen dead.
MID_EV30_024_m01_037: Then again, they know less of their foe. We have a\ngood deal more experience by now.
MID_EV30_024_m01_038: I detect an opportunity for us here. Let us put them\nsquarely in our debt.
MID_EV30_024_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_039: <NCA>"Let's not waste any time."
MID_EV30_024_m01_040: Hear, hear. We can't stand by and watch as the\nliving are slaughtered.
MID_EV30_024_m01_041: You there. Withdraw the survivors at once. We'll\nfinish what you started.
MID_EV30_024_m01_042: There is no shame in retreating, General Klapka.\nOur forces are fresh and capable.
MID_EV30_024_m01_043: What's this? A personal appearance from the\nqueen of Saramis?
MID_EV30_024_m01_044: I don't believe it... You wouldn't happen to be the\nPromised One I've heard about, would you?
MID_EV30_024_m01_045: Amazing! The god of the Mosa must have answered\nmy prayers.
MID_EV30_024_m01_046: But damned if I'll let you claim all the glory. The\nMosa have a part to play in beating them back too!
MID_EV30_024_m01_047: All of you will die. All will be destroyed.
MID_EV30_024_m01_048: Are you the gatekeeper here, then? We must insist\non your removal.
MID_EV30_024_m01_049: Ah! I know the regalia this Brimstone Lord wears...
MID_EV30_024_m01_050: His right arm...that gleaming, golden spear...\nCan it truly be?!
MID_EV30_024_m01_051: Are you Mahadu, the mightiest warrior of\nSaraminian legend?
MID_EV30_024_m01_052: Your Majesty, it goes further than that. Take another\nlook at the uniforms of his soldiers.
MID_EV30_024_m01_053: They predate even the ancient time of Mahadu...
MID_EV30_024_m01_054: Are you suggesting that these are the risen dead\nof Damascar?!
MID_EV30_024_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_024_m01_057: You... You are on the side of the Dagdan Empire,\nI expect.
MID_EV30_024_m01_058: <NCA>"I'm truly not."
MID_EV30_024_m01_059: This one owes allegiance to no banner, nation, or any\nother such fetter that binds humans.
MID_EV30_024_m01_060: You look upon the Promised One, who will rout you\nhere and guide the living to salvation.
MID_EV30_024_m01_061: No one who bears the stench of the gods should dare\nspeak to me of salvation.
MID_EV30_024_m01_062: I'll peel back that mask and show the world the\ntrue colors underneath.
MID_EV30_024_m01_063: Of all the foes we could have faced here, I had not\nexpected my vengeful ancestors.
MID_EV30_024_m01_064: But if it falls to me to stop you, then so I shall.
MID_EV30_024_m01_065: I battle here today to put the souls of my ancestors\nto their final rest!
MID_EV30_024_m01_066: Dagda the Great and his rotten empire trampled on\nthe future of Damascar...
MID_EV30_024_m01_067: Now I will return all the fury they cultivated at the\ntip of my spear!
MID_EV30_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_025_m01_001: I cannot believe it. The great Mahadu has been\nbested by the living.
MID_EV30_025_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_002: There is no denying it. You are true warriors to\nthe core.
MID_EV30_025_m01_003: I can feel myself crumbling... I wonder where I am\nheaded from here.
MID_EV30_025_m01_004: You endured much at Dagda's hands, not least the\nCleansing of Damascar.
MID_EV30_025_m01_005: I think that your anger is justified.
MID_EV30_025_m01_006: But you must still answer for the way you turned\nyour righteous fury on the living.
MID_EV30_025_m01_007: You did willingly follow Balor, bringing calamity\nupon this land.
MID_EV30_025_m01_008: That is a crime against all those who still live.
MID_EV30_025_m01_009: Ngh... She said you are called the Promised One?
MID_EV30_025_m01_010: You have my thanks. It was my good fortune to fight\npeople like you at the end.
MID_EV30_025_m01_011: <NCA>"I feel the same way."
MID_EV30_025_m01_012: You should be proud. Only true heroes could defeat\nthe likes of me.
MID_EV30_025_m01_013: May you rest peacefully, my ancestors. Know that I\nwill carry out your dying wishes.
MID_EV30_025_m01_014: Your regrets and your anger will not be forgotten.
MID_EV30_025_m01_015: However, strength born of rage is no way to secure\na path forward.
MID_EV30_025_m01_016: Especially when that rage has been stoked by Balor.
MID_EV30_025_m01_017: Hear me, my ancestors. Balor has no use for you—\nonly for your fury.
MID_EV30_025_m01_018: We are not made to live according to the will\nof another.
MID_EV30_025_m01_019: My life—my thoughts—will be my own. I shall take\npride in my choices, because I made them.
MID_EV30_025_m01_020: Then live on, descendant of ours.
MID_EV30_025_m01_021: I am pleased to have someone like you to carry\nforward our long-held dreams...
MID_EV30_025_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_022: Ahhh...
MID_EV30_025_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_023: At the end, they smiled.
MID_EV30_025_m01_024: That was fascinating. Guess it all worked out?
MID_EV30_025_m01_025: I suppose so. When they died, they all seemed\ncontented somehow.
MID_EV30_025_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_029: I do not think they will return to Balor. 
MID_EV30_025_m01_030: I'll pray that their regrets and anger be soothed as\nthey return to the great cycle.
MID_EV30_025_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_034: I once sought the power to overcome any obstacle.\nIn answer, Mahadu granted me this arm.
MID_EV30_025_m01_035: I believed that his power would open all paths to me.
MID_EV30_025_m01_036: But in the Heroic Games—and in the battles we have\nall fought together—I found new perspectives.
MID_EV30_025_m01_037: You all taught me that righteous fury alone\nwas insufficient.
MID_EV30_025_m01_038: Had I not learned that lesson, I very well could have\nbeen among their number.
MID_EV30_025_m01_039: I owe all of you a great deal. Particularly you,\nPromised One.
MID_EV30_025_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_025_m01_052: <NCA>"Do you really think they were saved?"
MID_EV30_025_m01_053: I can't speak with certainty. But I can at the very\nleast pray 'tis so.
MID_EV30_025_m01_054: The spirits of those who die harboring regrets are\nripe for capture by the underworld.
MID_EV30_025_m01_055: 'Tis a wretched thing that Balor takes advantage of\nthese wayward souls.
MID_EV30_025_m01_056: Now, we have unfinished business of our own here,\nI believe.
MID_EV30_122_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_122_m01_001: Hold right there! You're the person they call the\nPromised One, aren't you?
MID_EV30_122_m01_002: Hahaha! It wasn't easy to track you down in an\nunfamiliar land, but I've finally caught up to you.
MID_EV30_122_m01_003: <NCA>"And you are...?"
MID_EV30_122_m01_004: My name is Klapka. I'm a general of the glorious\nMosa Holy State.
MID_EV30_122_m01_005: Your feats in the recent struggle against the\nunderworld turned the tide.
MID_EV30_122_m01_006: The risen dead pouring from that gate crossed over\ninto Mosa territory, laying waste to all as they went.
MID_EV30_122_m01_007: Our country suffered terribly as a result. Only after\nyour arrival did things begin to look up.
MID_EV30_122_m01_008: Even the magnificent King Oktar expressed deep\ngratitude for your efforts.
MID_EV30_122_m01_009: In fact, he saw it as a perfect opportunity to forge an\nalliance with our long-time enemy of Saramis.
MID_EV30_122_m01_010: Part of that involved supplying matériel and troops\nto bring this war to a swift end.
MID_EV30_122_m01_011: Which is why I stand before you today.
MID_EV30_122_m01_012: <NCA>"You're alright with this?"
MID_EV30_122_m01_013: <NCB>"I suspect an ulterior motive."
MID_EV30_122_m01_014: <ACA>I have no quarrel with you. I know how I look, but\nI'm renowned for my honor as a general.
MID_EV30_122_m01_015: <ACA>I'm willing to follow whatever orders you issue.\nThough...I can only speak for myself there.
MID_EV30_122_m01_016: <ACB>A keen observation. I can't say you're entirely\nwrong there.
MID_EV30_122_m01_017: <ACB>How to put this delicately...our king's motives are\nnot what you might call "ulterior."
MID_EV30_122_m01_018: Between you and me, our king hates being bored\nmore than anything. It makes him a fickle man.
MID_EV30_122_m01_019: He's known to be untrustworthy at times, changing\nhis mind as the winds shift.
MID_EV30_122_m01_020: I wouldn't blame you for thinking he mostly sent help\nso that he can take the credit for success.
MID_EV30_122_m01_021: That all the matériel and troops he sent are just his\nway of hogging the glory.
MID_EV30_122_m01_022: In my opinion, you'd be right to think that.
MID_EV30_122_m01_023: But I think it unlikely he would betray you before the\nsituation was resolved in his favor.
MID_EV30_122_m01_024: But that's my king we're speaking of, and he isn't\nhere. I am.
MID_EV30_122_m01_025: And on my honor, I mean to repay the serious debt\nof gratitude I owe to you all.
MID_EV30_122_m01_026: <NCA>"Thank you."
MID_EV30_122_m01_027: Of course! And thank you for having me.
MID_EV30_122_m01_028: I'll put my life on the line, the same as any other\nsoldier at your command. You won't be disappointed.
MID_EV30_122_m01_029: All that aside...why is this city so huge? I've never\nseen anything like it.
MID_EV30_122_m01_030: It's grand enough to make a man's teeth fall out\nfrom the shock of it all. Hahaha!
MID_EV30_122_m01_031: Ah, but I'd better not tell King Oktar. He'd only\nbe jealous.
MID_EV30_122_m01_032: Knowing him, he might order an immediate\nrenovation of Halkaparikke.
MID_EV30_122_m01_033: Yes...best that I leave all this grandeur out of\nmy reports.
MID_EV30_019_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_019_m01_001: The gate we're after has manifested here at\nFort Hecatoncheires.
MID_EV30_019_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_082: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_083: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_084: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_085: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_086: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_087: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_002: There were odd reports about the way in which\nthe settlements in this area fell.
MID_EV30_019_m01_003: The towns and villages here seem not to have\nresisted their fate.
MID_EV30_019_m01_004: How can that be? Does that mean they\nkilled themselves?
MID_EV30_019_m01_005: Even if they couldn't muster an army, it seems like\nthey'd at least resist...or flee.
MID_EV30_019_m01_006: This can't be the whole story.
MID_EV30_019_m01_007: Have you received any further explanation for that?
MID_EV30_019_m01_008: No. The only halfway plausible theory is that they\nopened their gates to simply let the enemy in.
MID_EV30_019_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_009: <NCA>"What's your view on it?"
MID_EV30_019_m01_010: There is precious little to speculate from, but it may\nbe the power of the Brimstone Lord posted here.
MID_EV30_019_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_016: Promised One, I believe this may fall into my area\nof expertise.
MID_EV30_019_m01_017: <NCA>"What do you mean?"
MID_EV30_019_m01_018: I've heard rumors that there's a powerful spellsong\nuser among the enemies here.
MID_EV30_019_m01_019: There's a woman I can think of who might be\nguarding this gate.
MID_EV30_019_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_022: Hm. Let's all stay alert.
MID_EV30_019_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_027: What are those lovely tones? Ahhh.
MID_EV30_019_m01_028: Whoa, whoa, you can't just break ranks like that!
MID_EV30_019_m01_029: Hey! You're headed straight for the sea!
MID_EV30_019_m01_030: Mm? Yeah... The sea...
MID_EV30_019_m01_031: I've got to be in the sea too... Hehe... Hehe!
MID_EV30_019_m01_032: Hmhmhmhm.
MID_EV30_019_m01_033: It's a cruel world for living things, filled with\nsuffering at every turn.
MID_EV30_019_m01_034: May the pleasant fog of my music help you slip\ngently into the underworld.
MID_EV30_019_m01_035: Hm?!
MID_EV30_019_m01_036: Is someone...blocking my spellsong?
MID_EV30_019_m01_037: What was I doing? And why was I walking toward\nthe sea?
MID_EV30_019_m01_038: You too? I suddenly had a feeling there was\nsomething amazing waiting for me there.
MID_EV30_019_m01_039: So, the Promised One and their entourage. I can tell\nthere's something special about you.
MID_EV30_019_m01_040: You are not without talent yourself, but this show\nof yours is over.
MID_EV30_019_m01_041: <NCA>"You may as well accept defeat now."
MID_EV30_019_m01_042: Indeed. You are the gatekeeper here, yes?
MID_EV30_019_m01_043: I suggest you surrender peacefully so that we may\ndestroy the gate.
MID_EV30_019_m01_044: No, thank you. Balor would be ever so displeased\nwith me for that.
MID_EV30_019_m01_088: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_046: This Brimstone Lord has an air of refinement to him.
MID_EV30_019_m01_047: He is unfamiliar to me, but he strikes me as having\nbeen an incurable rake in life.
MID_EV30_019_m01_048: Suffice to say, he is not my type.
MID_EV30_019_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_049: His vihuela—it looks just like mine! He has his\nown Obsidian.
MID_EV30_019_m01_050: That means he must be... Ah!
MID_EV30_019_m01_051: If my performance didn't captivate you, then there\nis clearly no art in your souls.
MID_EV30_019_m01_052: But you won't resist my magnum opus—an even\nmore bewitching melody.
MID_EV30_019_m01_053: I'm not going to allow that.
MID_EV30_019_m01_054: The power at her fingertips... It's serving as a counter\nto my spellsong.
MID_EV30_019_m01_055: Is that Obsidian you're playing? Who are you to take\nup such an instrument?
MID_EV30_019_m01_056: You must be the legendary bard Cohen. Didn't you\ndie by hurling yourself into the sea?
MID_EV30_019_m01_057: I'd rather have met you while you were alive,\nand not...like this.
MID_EV30_019_m01_058: But I'm happy to bid you farewell with a song.
MID_EV30_019_m01_059: Ah...so my blood flows through your veins.
MID_EV30_019_m01_060: Then you ought to be at my side. The beauty of your\nsong more than earns you the right.
MID_EV30_019_m01_061: That loveliness could be preserved for eternity in\nmy paradise.
MID_EV30_019_m01_062: I know you've been twisted by Balor, but it still hurts\nto see my ancestor like this.
MID_EV30_019_m01_063: Anyway, I'll have to pass. I have too much to live\nfor here.
MID_EV30_019_m01_064: I'm going to send you back to the underworld,\nbefore you can soil my image of you any further.
MID_EV30_019_m01_065: Not if I have a say in the matter. My power is easily\na counter for yours.
MID_EV30_019_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_019_m01_071: Allow me to play a requiem from the heart for\nyou all.
MID_EV30_019_m01_072: No musician in the world is finer than I. Before we're\nthrough, I'll send the proof through your very souls.
MID_EV30_019_m01_073: Only then can you die at the hands of all the comely\nwomen I have loved.
MID_EV30_019_m01_074: Listen well! Do not be tempted by whatever this\nman promises you.
MID_EV30_019_m01_075: Even in his demigod days, he was close to divine.\nBalor's influence can only have strengthened him.
MID_EV30_019_m01_076: Ugh. 'Tis never simple with these gatekeepers. We'll\nhave to watch our steps around him.
MID_EV30_020_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_020_m01_001: Impossible... How could Obsidian fail when it was\nmade from Balor himself?
MID_EV30_020_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_082: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_002: Its strings are fraying... No! Damn it all. I can still\nplay... I can still...
MID_EV30_020_m01_003: <NCA>"Just give in."
MID_EV30_020_m01_004: I concur. You should give up and stand aside so we\ncan reach the underworld gate.
MID_EV30_020_m01_005: This doesn't count... I didn't lose. It was Obsidian\nthat failed, not me...
MID_EV30_020_m01_006: You did play beautifully...
MID_EV30_020_m01_007: Though, I have to say, a little mechanically. Your\nplaying lacked heart.
MID_EV30_020_m01_008: Bards make music for the living.
MID_EV30_020_m01_009: It's because of my attachment to the living world that\nI can reach people in their souls.
MID_EV30_020_m01_010: You reject life, so your music is lifeless, and it leaves\nthe heart unmoved.
MID_EV30_020_m01_011: Even now I cannot surpass her... Maria as she was\nback then.
MID_EV30_020_m01_012: She shocked me with skill that outmatched mine,\nand I admit, I was jealous.
MID_EV30_020_m01_013: Swearing that I would one day get good enough to\noutplay her, I parted company with her.
MID_EV30_020_m01_014: But I told her that we'd reunite once I'd reached the\nlevel of skill I sought.
MID_EV30_020_m01_015: That was when Maria loaned me Obsidian, to remind\nme of the promise I made.
MID_EV30_020_m01_016: But I could never rise to her level.
MID_EV30_020_m01_017: No matter how much of my soul I poured into my\ninstrument, I never surpassed what she could do.
MID_EV30_020_m01_018: It was worse than death. I couldn't stand it!
MID_EV30_020_m01_084: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_019: I cannot fathom the depths of this bitterness over\nyour skill with an instrument.
MID_EV30_020_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_021: I see my feelings are too complex for the likes of you\nto ever understand.
MID_EV30_020_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_023: Did you really have to put yourself through all that?
MID_EV30_020_m01_024: You might not have accepted yourself, but it's clear\nMaria loved you.
MID_EV30_020_m01_025: Who knows what different path she might have\ntaken, if you had stayed?
MID_EV30_020_m01_026: She was clinging to you the whole time... That's why\nwe saw her at Cohen's Mausoleum.
MID_EV30_020_m01_083: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_027: No more... I don't want to be in this world anymore.
MID_EV30_020_m01_085: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_031: Ah...
MID_EV30_020_m01_032: <NCA>"What's wrong?"
MID_EV30_020_m01_033: I don't understand. Why torture yourself trying to be\nbetter than everyone else?
MID_EV30_020_m01_034: Men! Idiots. This is why I can't stand them.
MID_EV30_020_m01_035: They boil everything in life down to two things—\nwinning and losing.
MID_EV30_020_m01_036: I'm not a man, and I can actually understand\nhis mindset.
MID_EV30_020_m01_037: It's fine in your case, since you don't cause trouble\nfor anyone other than me.
MID_EV30_020_m01_038: A musician should play because they want to, not out\nof some misguided competitiveness.
MID_EV30_020_m01_039: I still remember, the first time I held an instrument,\nthe sense of inspiration it gave me. Still gives me.
MID_EV30_020_m01_040: Over time, I learned the instrument well enough that\nI could express in song what I felt inside.
MID_EV30_020_m01_041: My emotions, my passions...who I was.
MID_EV30_020_m01_042: From then on, I was captivated forever.
MID_EV30_020_m01_043: I was playing for the joy of expression, nothing else.
MID_EV30_020_m01_044: Now you sound arrogant, Leilidahna. Not all of us\ncan embrace music with that unalloyed pleasure.
MID_EV30_020_m01_045: No matter, I suppose that's what makes you my rival.\nThe one I will work tirelessly to surpass!
MID_EV30_020_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_053: Looking at the risen dead, sometimes I couldn't help\nbut wonder...
MID_EV30_020_m01_054: The world's such a horrible place to live, full of pain\nand suffering.
MID_EV30_020_m01_055: Maybe it would be easier—dying, coming back as\none of them—and not having to deal with all that.
MID_EV30_020_m01_056: I get it. Death can be scary, but...
MID_EV30_020_m01_057: some people think of it as a relief.
MID_EV30_020_m01_058: You don't have to be afraid when you're dead. Seems\nlike more and more people think that way.
MID_EV30_020_m01_059: And I've got no clue what to say to those who feel\nlike that.
MID_EV30_020_m01_060: Well, I've come to realize there's something hollow\nabout them. The risen dead.
MID_EV30_020_m01_061: You're almost fooled into thinking they're the people\nthey were, but they only look the same.
MID_EV30_020_m01_062: Their regrets and resentments from life have been\namplified and twisted by Balor.
MID_EV30_020_m01_063: They're empty shells that say and do the same things\nover and over.
MID_EV30_020_m01_064: I don't want to end up like that.
MID_EV30_020_m01_065: So, I'm going to survive. I have no doubts about\nthat anymore.
MID_EV30_020_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_020_m01_069: Listen to that voice that urges you to live.
MID_EV30_020_m01_070: The work of living is not something one does to\nsatisfy others' demands.
MID_EV30_020_m01_071: None will deny that it can be an uncertain and\npainful thing.
MID_EV30_020_m01_072: But I believe 'tis this very pain that imparts the work\nwith meaning.
MID_EV30_020_m01_073: Where will a life of struggle lead? Perhaps that is the\nanswer the progenitor god seeks from us.
MID_EV30_119_m01: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_001: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_002: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_003: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_004: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_005: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_006: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_017: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_119_m01_024: 
